(9) examination of drugs and devices and treatment of those found to be unacceptable as defined by the board;
(10) due diligence regarding other trading partners;
(11) creation and maintenance of records, including transaction records;
(12) procedures for operation; and
(13) procedures for compliance with the requirements of the federal drug supply chain security act, 21 U.S.C. § 351 et seq.
(i) This section shall be part of and supplemental to the pharmacy act of the state of Kansas.
